# ClauseIQ Design System (UI)

Canonical source: `frontend/src/index.css` — **ClauseIQ Design System v1.2** (tokens 19 Jun 2026; Typography Concept C 31 Jul 2026). Do not invent new hex values; extend tokens in `index.css` only with owner approval. Components use `var(--*)` only.

## Tokens

- Colors: `var(--color-*)` only in components (bg, text, border, accent, alert, success, warning, ai, priority, z-index).
- Text hierarchy: `--color-text-primary` / `--secondary` / `--tertiary` (no opacity hacks for muted copy).
- Prefer CSS variables over Tailwind arbitrary colors (`bg-[#…]`, `hover:bg-[rgba(…)]`).
- Tailwind `theme.extend.colors` in `tailwind.config.js` mirrors the palette — do not introduce a third hex set.
- No fallback hex outside the palette.

## Typography (Concept C)

| Role | Token | Typical size |
|------|--------|----------------|
| Brand Stage (Login only) | `--font-brand` | `--type-brand-stage` (~48) |
| Page H1 | `--font-brand` | `--type-h1` (22) |
| Module / authoring H1 | `--font-brand` | `--type-h1-module` (20) |
| Section H2 | `--font-brand` | `--type-h2` (18) |
| Card / panel title | `--font-brand` | `--type-title-card` (16) |
| UI body / controls | `--font-ui` | 12–13 |
| Meta / chips / labels | `--font-ui` or `--font-meta` | 11 |
| IDs, numbers, lang toggle | `--font-meta` | 11 |
| Letter / RFI body (TipTap only) | `--font-document` | body |

Do **not** use `--font-brand` at ≤14px. Do not use `--font-document` outside the authoring editor surface.

## Signature accent (gold-line)

- Color always `var(--color-accent)`.
- Use `.gold-line` + size class — do not paste inline gradients:
  - `.gold-line-stage` — 96px (Login Brand Stage)
  - `.gold-line-nav` — 32px (app chrome)
  - `.gold-line-compact` — 20px (workspace / detail breadcrumbs)

## Reference gutter

One measure for the record number across the whole app: `--gutter-ref` (104px). Use it for the "No." column in every list grid and for the ref slot in overview rows — never a literal pixel value or a Tailwind width. Status columns get `--gutter-status`; it is sized for the widest translated chip, so a narrower literal will clip the label.

- `.ref-number` — the only treatment for a record number, anywhere it appears (list column, detail eyebrow, chain stop, nav breadcrumb, relation row). Carries `tabular-nums`; do not restate font/size/letter-spacing inline.
- **The reference cell holds the reference and nothing else.** Response arrows, RES/REV badges and any other marker belong beside the subject, where the `1fr` track can absorb them. Packing them into the gutter is what makes the number collide with the next column on chain-indented rows.
- `.data-figure` — dates and amounts sitting in a scanned column. Colour stays with the caller so overdue rows can still go red. It is `nowrap` and clips, so it takes the figure only — a status word appended to a date goes in its own span.
- Proportional figures in a column of numbers are a defect: if it is a date or an identifier being compared down a column, it gets one of these two classes.

## List row geometry

Grid and flex children resolve to `min-width: auto`, so a `nowrap` cell grows past its declared track and renders over its neighbour instead of being held by the column. The track definition alone does not constrain anything.

- Every fixed-column list row (and its header) carries `className="list-row"`. That is the only thing putting `min-width: 0` on its cells; without it the columns are advisory.
- A chain-indented child adds 16px of left padding, which comes out of the reference track. Size the gutter for the longest real reference **plus** that indent, not for the parent row alone.
- In a `space-between` flex row, the text side needs `minWidth: 0` and the action side needs `flexShrink: 0`. Otherwise a long subject pushes the buttons out of the row. This applies to the chain-child rows on detail pages, not just to lists.
- Layering: anything that must outrank another component takes a `--z-*` token — `--z-sticky` for sticky panels and rails, `--z-dropdown` for any menu or autocomplete. Single-digit raw values are fine for paper-stacking *inside* one component, and should stay below the token scale so a real dropdown always wins.

## Chain thread

The parent/child relationship is drawn, not implied by indentation. Never use a `└` text glyph.

- List: wrapper gets `.chain-branch`, the child row gets `.chain-node`. The thread and its elbow are pseudo-elements; the indent stays at 28px so the tick lands clear of the number.
- The 2px left rail carries **status** on every row, parent and child alike. Chain membership is the thread's job — do not overload the rail with both.
- Detail breadcrumb: `.chain-rail` wrapping `.chain-stop` items, current node `.chain-stop-current`. No arrow glyphs, no underlined links.
- Thread colour is `--color-accent-light`; it should read as quiet structure, not as an accent.

## Workspace sidebar (file dividers)

- Left stack of modules = dossier tabs / file dividers (association, not literal tab shapes).
- Active item: **3px** left border `var(--color-accent)` + secondary fill (`.nav-item-active` pattern).
- Inactive: transparent 3px left border (alignment preserved). Never 4px.

## Geometry

- `borderRadius: 0` / `rounded-none` — sharp corners. Exception: `borderRadius: "50%"` for status **dots / count badges** only.
- Prefer flat borders over decorative `boxShadow` unless the surface already uses elevation tokens (`--color-shadow`).

## Patterns

- Inline styles + CSS variables (house style). Shared actions via `Button`; status via `StatusChip`.
- Deterministic CTA: `Button` (`rounded-none`). Intelligence CTA: `AiActionButton` / `.ai-action-btn` (radius 6, `--color-ai`). Compact graph launcher: `.ai-icon-btn`. Do not mix geometries.
- Filter chips: active text `var(--color-bg-primary)` — never raw parchment hex.
- Status chips map to `--color-alert-*` / `--color-success*` / `--color-warning*` / `--color-ai*`.
- `Button` variants: primary / secondary / destructive / **warning** (`--color-warning`, `--color-warning-wash`). Sizes: default **13px** (page CTA), sm **12px** (inline).
- List-row left ticks stay **2px**. Tabs / file-dividers stay **3px**. Do not unify.
- Print / letterhead WYSIWYG uses `--color-print-*` (defined only on `:root`, not `html.dark`).
- Destructive confirms use `ConfirmModal`, not `window.confirm`. Chrome nav: `.app-chrome-nav` (wraps on tablet). Detail künye: `.meta-grid-3` (3→2 col at 900px).
- Unsaved work: `useUnsavedGuard(active)` on any surface that holds server-unaccepted input.

## Language, dates, money

- Three languages: `tr` / `en` / `ar`. All user-facing copy goes through `t("key")` in `LanguageContext`; never hardcode a literal, and never write a two-branch `lang === "tr" ? … : …` for new strings.
- Every dictionary entry must carry all three languages. Enforced by `node scripts/check-i18n.mjs` — run it before UI sign-off.
- Chrome language control is `<LanguageToggle />` (segmented EN/TR/AR). No per-page toggle buttons.
- Arabic sets `dir="rtl"` on `<html>`. Arabic faces (Amiri, IBM Plex Sans Arabic) are **fallbacks appended** to the existing stacks — never swap fonts per language. Wrap Latin identifiers inside Arabic prose in `.ltr-inline`.
- Dates: `formatDateCompact()` (ISO) in scanned table columns, `formatDate()` / `formatDateTime()` in prose and detail fields. Money: `formatMoney()`. All from `utils/format.ts` — never bare `toLocaleDateString` / `toLocaleString`, which follow the reader's browser locale.
- Never surface raw system values (HTTP codes, enum keys, similarity floats). `StatusChip` resolves `status.*` keys; unmapped enums degrade to spaced text.
- Two record vocabularies, not interchangeable: `module.*` is the plural navigation name (sidebar, tabs, chart legend), `entity.*` is the singular name for one record in prose (alert rows, deadline rows). A server-supplied display label (`"CORR"`, `"DEL"`) is a fallback for unknown types only — resolve the machine `type` through the dictionary first.
- Charts are UI, not data dumps: series names, axis ticks and tooltip labels all go through `t()`. A legend reading `Correspondence` next to Arabic body copy is the same defect as a hardcoded string anywhere else.

## Absence vs failure

- A failed fetch must never render as an empty result set. Lists show `state.loadfailed` plus a retry control, distinct from the "no records" copy.
- A server-capped list shows `state.truncated` above the header row. Silent truncation is a false negative in a claim.

## Audit commands (re-run before UI sign-off)

```bash
# Hardcoded hex outside the token file
rg -n "#[0-9A-Fa-f]{3,8}\b" frontend/src -g "*.{tsx,ts,css}"

# Radius drift
rg -n "borderRadius:\s*[1-9]|rounded-sm|rounded-full|rounded-md|rounded-lg" frontend/src -g "*.{tsx,ts,css}"

# Font stacks
rg -n "fontFamily\s*:" frontend/src -g "*.{tsx,ts}"

# Brand at meta scale (should be empty for ≤14 with font-brand)
rg -n "font-brand.*fontSize:\s*1[0-4]|fontSize:\s*1[0-4].*font-brand" frontend/src -g "*.{tsx,ts}"

# Inline gold gradients (prefer .gold-line)
rg -n "linear-gradient\(to bottom" frontend/src -g "*.{tsx,ts}"

# Reference numbers not using the shared treatment
rg -n 'fontFamily: "var\(--font-meta\)", fontSize: 11' frontend/src -g "*.tsx"

# Hardcoded gutter width instead of --gutter-ref
rg -n '"90px"|w-24' frontend/src -g "*.tsx"

# Tree glyphs standing in for the chain thread
rg -n "└" frontend/src -g "*.tsx"
```

Type-check with `npx tsc -p tsconfig.app.json --noEmit` (or `npm run build`). A bare `npx tsc --noEmit` at the frontend root resolves the solution-style config and silently checks nothing.
